---
import DrawbridgeLayout from "@/layouts/DrawbridgeLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "@/components/drawbridge/PageHeader.astro";
import { Prose } from "@/components/starwind/prose";
---

<DrawbridgeLayout title="Privacy" description="Drawbridge privacy: imported files stay in your browser session.">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-3xl gap-8">
    <PageHeader title="Privacy" description="Your course files stay on your device and are never uploaded." />

    <Prose class="max-w-none text-foreground" style="--sw-prose-h2-size: 1.125rem;">
      <h2>What Drawbridge does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No server-side processing of imported files.</li>
        <li>No analytics or tracking.</li>
        <li>No cookies.</li>
        <li>No account or login.</li>
        <li>No database or browser storage for imported course data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How course imports work</h2>
      <p>
        Drawbridge is a static site. Your browser downloads the site's pages and code, then processes any file you
        choose locally and in memory. Course content is not sent over the network.
      </p>
      <p>
        Moving between connected tools keeps the opened course in the current browser session. Refreshing the page,
        opening a separate tab, closing the tab, or choosing <strong>Close course</strong> forgets the imported data.
      </p>
      <p>
        A restrictive Content Security Policy limits connections to the Drawbridge site itself. Course HTML is also
        rebuilt against a safe allowlist, and externally hosted course images are not loaded.
      </p>

      <h2>Offline use</h2>
      <p>
        Drawbridge is an installable progressive web app. After the first load, a service worker caches the Drawbridge
        site so it can work without a network connection. This cache contains the application, not your imported
        courses. Clearing the site's cached data does not affect the privacy of a course session.
      </p>

      <h2>Recommendations for sensitive data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use a private or incognito browser window when appropriate.</li>
        <li>Disable browser extensions you do not trust.</li>
        <li>Turn off your network connection after loading the site for an extra layer of assurance.</li>
        <li>Close the course or the tab when you are finished.</li>
      </ul>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</DrawbridgeLayout>
